# Run BOTH APIs first. Uses a token from the Identity API.
@identity = https://localhost:7263
@hms = https://localhost:7109

### Health - should say Healthy
GET {{hms}}/health

### Get a DEV token (receptionist "dev", Swetha)
# @name devToken
POST {{identity}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Any valid token -> 200
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### Front Desk licensed + REGISTRATION_CREATE -> 200
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/front-desk
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### Admin-only permission -> 403 for a receptionist
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/all-collections
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### Doctor module not licensed in this token -> 403
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/doctor
Authorization: Bearer {{devToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### No token -> 401
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/whoami

### Get an ADMIN token (all permissions + Doctor module), then retry the 403 calls with it
# @name adminToken
POST {{identity}}/api/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": 3,
  "userName": "priya",
  "displayName": "Priya",
  "roles": ["Admin"],
  "permissions": ["PATIENT_VIEW","PATIENT_CREATE","PATIENT_EDIT","REGISTRATION_CREATE","PAYMENT_COLLECT","QUEUE_VIEW","COLLECTION_VIEW_ALL"],
  "modules": ["REGISTRATION","BILLING","DOCTOR","NURSE","PHARMACY","LAB","PAYROLL"]
}

### Admin -> 200
GET {{hms}}/api/platform-check/all-collections
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.accessToken}}
